    "q-108278": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108278",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(4),$ calculate $P(X<9).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{9}x{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x≈3.75560\n$$\n\n*The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A chi-square random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(k)$ with $k$ degrees of freedom has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(4).$ So, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4Γ(2)}x{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecalling that $Γ(n)=(n-1)!$ for any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(2)=1!=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the probability distribution becomes\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}x{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $P(X<9)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<9) & ={\\int }_{0}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{9}\\frac{1}{4}x{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{9}x{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ≈\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 3.75560 \\\\  & =0.9389\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
